First, never nurse dance.  It seems like a good idea, but it's not
worth the risk.  I've lost one promising game to this, and an AoLS
another time.  If you need more hitpoints, foocubus dancing and
alchemy are safer.

Although I haven't done this since, in my first ascension, I kept
a large number of paper and pencil notes, both on things I'd seen
(e.g. "minetown branch on dlvl3", "temple on dlvl18") and goals
to accomplish, in rough order of priority ("get reflection",
"get fire resistance", "improve AC", "need spare AoLS", etc.)
I'm not sure if it was the organization of just the fact that
keeping this list forced me to play slowly and carefully, but
for whatever reason, it worked.  I still keep *some* notes, just
not the detailed priority list.

In some of your later posts, you seemed overly concerned about
generating too many artifacts.  This isn't all bad; it's a stupid
idea to make Sting, for example, but for Odin's sake, get Mojo
and your quest artifact as soon as you can.  Having spare wishes
that might not give you an artifact because you have 15 of the things
already is a problem you *want* to have.  Just don't sacrifice too
much after you've got Mojo and you'll have good odds of getting
an artifact with a wish.

Also, take your time and clear out every level.  You'll get
experience (and once you hit dlvl20 or so, having a low level
isn't going to make the monsters that much easier, so don't
stay low level for that reason.)  And you'll get more gear.
And you'll have safe levels to retreat to.

Finally, don't plan *too* far ahead. Specifically, don't plan
for anything after the castle.  Spend your resources to get
to the castle.  You'll find replacements in the random gear
and the wand will pick up the difference.  Just maximize your
chances of getting *to* the castle and you'll maximize your
chances of winning the game.  It's really rare for monsters
to surround you in Gehennom, since it's mostly mazes, so it's
actually *easier* than the levels before the castle.  You can
ask for more specific advice once you get to that point if you
still need it.




